    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval is seeking an artificial intelligence solution to improve the efficiency of The City of Belval administrative services and quality of service rendered to users. The project has a duration of 4 years, with a global budget allocated at 3 million euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The annual cost of exploitation must remain compatible with The City of Belval budgetary capacities. How can we consolidate we agents' contributions into a coherent tender response that addresses these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As Project Coordinator Agent for Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that Nexus Engineering has experience in AI solutions, which aligns with The City of Belval requirements. Nexus Engineering have previously worked on similar projects, such as the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering project management capabilities include PRINCE2 and Agile Scrum methodologies, and Nexus Engineering have a team of certified project managers, including 5 PMP-certified PMs. Nexus Engineering typical delivery structure includes phases like Inception & Design, Pilot/MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering can leverage Nexus Engineering expertise in AI solutions and digital transformation to design an intelligent assistance tool for the municipal agents. an intelligent assistance tool for the municipal agents could integrate with existing systems, such as business software and electronic document management, using API-type interfaces. Regarding budget constraints, Nexus Engineering have experience managing large projects, with Nexus Engineering largest project managed being 4.5 million euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering can work within the allocated budget of 3 million euros over 4 years to provide a cost-effective solution. Nexus Engineering change management capabilities include dedicated change managers and training delivery options like in-person workshops and e-learning, which would help ensure a smooth transition for the municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, Nexus Engineering risk management approach includes maintaining a risk register and reviewing risks bi-weekly, which will help identify potential issues early on. Nexus Engineering also prioritize low-to-medium risk appetite, ensuring that Nexus Engineering take calculated decisions to minimize potential threats." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering consortium experience, having led 8 consortia with up to 5 partners, could be beneficial if Nexus Engineering decide to partner with other companies to deliver The project. One of Nexus Engineering known partners, LexIA GmbH, has expertise in Legal AI and regulatory compliance engines, which might be useful in addressing The City of Belval regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, by leveraging Nexus Engineering strengths in AI solutions, digital transformation, and project management, Nexus Engineering can develop a comprehensive tender response that addresses The City of Belval requirements while ensuring compatibility with The City of Belval budgetary constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide times of response compatible with daily use by agents, with an expected time of response lower than 2 seconds." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should also guarantee a high level of availability (99.9%) and integrate with existing systems of information, including business software and electronic management of documents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current technical architecture meet these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the performance benchmarks typical for our company, our have achieved a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG solutions, which is below the expected time of response of 2 seconds." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG solutions, which is below the expected time of response of 2 seconds does not directly translate to the specific use case described in the Call for Tenders, and further evaluation would be necessary to confirm whether our solution can meet this requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding availability, our have achieved an availability of 99.92% on past projects, which exceeds the expected level of availability of 99.9%. achieved suggests that our current technical architecture is capable of meeting the availability requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration with existing systems of information, our has experience with API standards such as REST and GraphQL, and our have worked with API gateways like Kong and Apigee. our also have experience with message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ, and with GED systems like Alfresco and OpenKM." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "While this does not guarantee seamless integration with the specific systems used by the City of Belval, this suggests that our current technical architecture is capable of meeting the integration requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, based on the information available in our company context, it appears that our current technical architecture can meet the requirements for response time, availability, and integration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, further evaluation and testing would be necessary to confirm meet and ensure that our solution meets the specific needs of the City of Belval." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must respect regulatory requirements in force, including the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). The solution should ensure strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), hosting data exclusively within the European Union, with no transfer outside the European Union, and protecting sensitive data through encryption or anonymization." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure we security and compliance posture meets these constraints? As Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has experience with the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) compliance, having a appointed Data Protection Officer (DPO) and contact email dpo@nexus-engineering.it." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have a standard data residency policy of hosting data exclusively within the European Union, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. prohibit cross-border transfers by default unless there is an explicit legal basis. To protect sensitive data, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have implemented various data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are also capable of conducting Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA), with an average duration of 3 weeks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding security controls, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have experience designing role-based access control (RBAC). Nexus Engineering S.r.l. network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have a Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) system in place, with real-time integration and log immutability using SHA-256 hash chaining. To ensure we AI-powered solution meets the GDPR requirements, we have implemented specific AI security controls, including prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation, and model update security review." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging these existing capabilities and experience, we can ensure that our AI-powered solution meets the required regulatory constraints, including strict compliance with the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) and data protection requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation of an agent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should provide explainability and transparency in The solution recommendations and proposals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the regulatory requirements outlined in the call for tenders?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on we company context, we note that The solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation of an agent, which aligns with we policy of no automated decision without human validation. we also have expertise in EU AI Act, prohibited AI practices awareness, limited risk AI transparency obligations, and human oversight contractual enforcement, which should help we meet the explainability and transparency requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for regulatory compliance, we are aware of the need to respect the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) and have a standard legal basis for data processing under Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest. we also have a data protection agreement template version 3.2 and can provide support for data protection impact assessments." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, we should flag the risk of the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) non-compliance if we subcontractors or suppliers are not properly vetted, as we require all subcontractors to be EU-established. we should ensure that we subcontracting policy is strictly adhered to, with a thorough legal and financial due diligence process, including exclusion grounds checks for any potential subcontractors." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, as we have expertise in open-source license compliance, we should review the licenses used in The solution to ensure the licenses used in the solution are compatible with commercial use and do not pose any risks. we standard licenses used are Apache 2.0, MIT, and LGPL v2.1, which should be cleared for commercial use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while we appear to be generally compliant with the regulatory requirements outlined in the call for tenders, we must carefully review we subcontracting policy, data protection measures, and open-source license compliance to mitigate any potential legal risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain mastered and compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected, and what is we projected margin on this contract?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given The global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, The global budget allocated to the project averages to 750,000 euros per year. we tender eligibility indicates we are eligible for contracts up to 3 million euros, so we can bid on the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs while guaranteeing quality of service, we would need to ensure we pricing model aligns with the client's expectations and we own cost structure. we standard daily rates range from 550 to 1050 euros per day, depending on the role." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without knowing the exact scope of work and the roles required, it's difficult to provide a precise cost optimization plan. we target gross margin percentage is 28%, and we minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Assuming we can deliver the project within these margins, we projected revenue would be 750,000 euros per year." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "If we achieve we target gross margin of 28%, we projected profit would be 210,000 euros per year." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, this calculation does not take into account we fixed and variable costs, which are 35% and 65% of the project cost respectively." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
