        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, facilitating access to information, improving the quality of answers, and reducing processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should also integrate with existing practices and not constitute a rupture in municipal agents modes of work." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy can we propose to meet these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, we proposed solution will leverage we expertise in large language models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation capabilities. we can deploy we preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong performance in French-language tasks and is self-hostable, ensuring compliance with EU data protection regulations. we AI components will include a combination of natural language processing and information retrieval techniques to facilitate access to internal procedures, regulatory texts, and relevant documents. our proposed solution will utilize we Retrieval-Augmented Generation capabilities, featuring dense vector semantic search and hybrid retrieval strategies, to provide accurate and context-specific answers to agents' queries." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To improve the quality of answers and reduce processing times, we can fine-tune our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong performance in French-language tasks and is self-hostable using we LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus, achieving an average accuracy gain of 12%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk80> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we will implement quantization methods such as INT8 to optimize energy consumption while maintaining performance. we innovation strategy will focus on incremental development and testing, with a pilot phase on a limited scope followed by progressive generalization to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk81> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach aligns with we typical V1 to V2 development timeline of 9 months, allowing for agile adaptation to user feedback and evolving requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk82> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explainability and transparency, we will incorporate source citation and chain-of-thought display capabilities into our proposed solution, enabling agents to understand the reasoning behind the provided answers and suggestions. we confidence scoring feature will also be implemented to detect low-confidence responses, triggering an uncertainty warning and escalation to human supervisors when necessary." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk83> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging we existing AI expertise and innovation pipeline, we can deliver a tailored solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for intelligent assistance, integration with existing practices, and compliance with regulatory constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk84> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to limit The City of Belval environmental footprint by proposing a solution that contributes to reducing energetic consumption and relies on infrastructures with low carbon impact. How can our CSR and sustainability posture support aims, and what strategies can our propose to minimize the environmental impact of our solution?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk85> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As the CSR and Sustainability Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can affirm that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has a strong commitment to reducing Nexus Engineering S.r.l. environmental footprint. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have already implemented various digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, which reduces GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk86> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, use 100% renewable energy and have low Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) values of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively. Our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, are also ISO14001 certified, which ensures Our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, commitment to environmental management." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk87> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To support aims, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose hosting our solution on these green infrastructures. Additionally, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. carbon reporting capability, based on GRI Standards (partial), will enable Nexus Engineering S.r.l. to monitor and report the carbon footprint of our solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk88> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. estimate that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which could contribute to minimizing the environmental impact of our solution. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can also propose strategies such as optimizing data storage, reducing data transfer, and using energy-efficient hardware to further minimize the environmental impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk89> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. e-waste management partner, Ecologic (France), is certified for WEEE recycling, ensuring responsible disposal of electronic waste. By leveraging Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing CSR and sustainability practices and proposing these strategies, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can support The City of Belval objective of reducing The City of Belval environmental footprint while providing a high-quality solution that meets The City of Belval needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk90> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# 1. Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is pleased to submit a comprehensive tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in municipal agents daily tasks, aligning with the City of Belval's digital transformation strategy. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily tasks, aligning with the City of Belval's digital transformation strategy leverages expertise in large language models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation capabilities, ensuring compliance with EU data protection regulations. # 2. Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval's requires an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and complies with regulatory constraints. an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and complies with regulatory constraints must provide quick access to reliable information, facilitate drafting administrative contents, assist in file analysis, and ensure collaboration and continuity among agents. # 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk91> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Proposed Solution Proposed Solution will utilize the Mistral 7B Instruct model, which offers strong performance in French-language tasks and is self-hostable, ensuring compliance with EU data protection regulations. The AI components will include a combination of natural language processing and information retrieval techniques to facilitate access to internal procedures, regulatory texts, and relevant documents. Proposed Solution will be designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation of an agent, aligning with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. policy of no automated decision without human validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk92> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement explainability and transparency features, including source citation and chain-of-thought display capabilities, enabling agents to understand the reasoning behind provided answers and suggestions. To ensure security and compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and implement role-based access control (RBAC). Nexus Engineering S.r.l. network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk93> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will also conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA) with an average duration of 3 weeks. The hosting will be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, with a particular attention to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, use 100% renewable energy and have low Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) values of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk94> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that will remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target a gross margin percentage of 28% and have a minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18%. # 4. Unaddressed Requirements The call for tenders requires the solution to provide times of response compatible with daily use by agents, with an indicative time of response lower than 2 seconds." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk95> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "While Nexus Engineering S.r.l. technical architecture has achieved a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG solutions, which is below the expected time of response, further evaluation would be necessary to confirm whether Proposed Solution can meet this requirement. # 5. Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident that Proposed Solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and complies with regulatory constraints. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are committed to delivering a high-quality solution that supports the City of Belval's digital transformation strategy while minimizing the City of Belval's environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk96> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. team is experienced in managing large projects, with a largest project managed being 4.5 million euros. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a team of certified project managers, including 5 PMP-certified PMs, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. typical delivery structure includes phases like Inception & Design, Pilot/MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe that Proposed Solution offers the best value for the City of Belval's and look forward to the opportunity to discuss Proposed Solution in further detail." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

